      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Specialized Carrier Decking &amp; Hydraulic Ramp Trailer Features for Bikaner‑Bagdogra Car Transport</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">**Technical Overview of Specialized Carrier Decking and Hydraulic‑Ramp Trailer for Bikaner‑to‑Bagdogra Car Transport**

The long‑haul vehicle transport between Bikaner and Bagdogra employs a state‑of‑the‑art multi‑car enclosed trailer, engineered to meet the stringent demands of high‑value car shifting services across this 1,500‑km corridor. The trailer’s core is a 20‑foot, 45‑foot modular deck that can accommodate up to six passenger cars or four SUVs, each secured by dual‑axis hydraulic ramp systems. The hydraulic ramps, rated at 15 kN per side, provide a smooth 5° incline that eliminates the risk of wheel‑to‑deck contact during loading and unloading, thereby preserving the vehicles’ pristine condition.

Load‑bearing capacity is a critical specification: the deck’s aluminum composite structure, reinforced with a 2.5 mm carbon‑fiber overlay, supports a maximum payload of 12 t (≈ 2,500 kg per car). Each car is further restrained by a custom‑fitted 4‑point tie‑down system that distributes weight evenly across the deck, preventing any single point from exceeding 500 kg. This design not only meets but exceeds the Indian Road Transport (IRT) regulations for inter‑state freight, ensuring compliance with both safety and legal standards.

Anti‑scratch deck surfaces are achieved through a dual‑layer coating: a base polyurethane layer that resists abrasion, topped with a micro‑toughened silica glaze. This combination reduces the coefficient of friction to 0.25, allowing vehicles to glide onto the deck without wheel‑scratches or paint damage—a vital feature for premium car shifting services. The deck also incorporates a drainage system that channels any accumulated moisture to a central sump, keeping the surface dry and reducing the risk of corrosion.

Real‑time GPS tracking is integrated into every trailer, providing a live feed of location, speed, and environmental parameters. The system’s geofencing capability alerts dispatchers if the trailer deviates from its planned route, ensuring that the vehicle transport remains on schedule and secure. Coupled with a built‑in dash‑cam and a remote diagnostic module, the fleet manager can monitor vehicle health and trailer integrity in real time.

In summary, the specialized carrier decking and hydraulic ramp trailer deliver a secure, efficient, and technologically advanced solution for Bikaner‑to‑Bagdogra vehicle transport. By combining robust load‑bearing capacity, anti‑scratch deck surfaces, and advanced GPS tracking, the system guarantees that each car arrives in pristine condition, supporting the broader ecosystem of open vehicle transport and car shifting services.</div>
